! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F211 "STORE LOW ORDER
! TEST ROUTINE", sub-tests A3-A4 (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf
! p.113, octal 016163.00-016201.00, where F211A5 begins).
!
! The first UNFLAGGED SLO, and so the first thing anywhere to exercise
! the instruction's headline rule: "the exponent is obtained by
! SUBTRACTING 48 from the exponent in bits 0-11 of the accumulator"
! (Ref. Manual p.97). F211A1-A2 are both flagged, where the
! accumulator's exponent is kept unchanged, so neither of them can see
! the subtraction at all.
!
! Both sub-tests are the same shape -- load a double, drop its own
! fraction into the low half with C0011 so the low 48 bits are known,
! store with SLO(U), and compare against a constant that is the same
! fraction at an exponent 48 lower:
!
!   A3  FPK28 is exponent +256, fraction ffffffffffff.
!       SLO(U) stores fraction ffffffffffff at exponent 256 - 48 = 208.
!       Expected FPK44: exponent +208, fraction ffffffffffff.
!       The listing says so itself -- "TEST RESULT EXP+208".
!   A4  FPK38 is exponent +50, fraction 555555555555.
!       SLO(U) stores it at 50 - 48 = 2.
!       Expected FPK39: exponent +2, fraction 555555555555.
!       The listing: "CHECK OPND WITH EXPONENT++2".
!
! A4 is the sharper of the two because its arithmetic is small enough
! to be unambiguous: an exponent of +2 can only have come from 50 - 48.
! A3's +208 confirms the same rule at a distance from zero.
!
! Both are SLO(U), so the normalization path -- and with it the noisy
! mode question that fpNormalize48 exists for -- is still unexercised.
! So is the generated-flag case, where subtracting 48 underflows and
! p.97 says normalization DOES occur. Those wait for later sub-tests.
!
! ROS (022355) is the routine's scratch word, not a pool constant.
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pools pp.176-177. PASS sits at 016201.00, where F211A5 begins.
!
! Instructions: DL(U), C0011, SLO(U), L, CT0110, SIC, BZB, BRGZ, B.
! verify_fp_arith_f211a3_4_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- the routine's scratch word --
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pools pp.176-177) --
        SLC, (8)022041.0
FPK28   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0200177777777777777760
        SLC, (8)022053.0
FPK38   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031052525252525252520
FPK39   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001052525252525252520
        SLC, (8)022061.0
FPK44   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0150177777777777777760

! The listing prints no label at 016163.00 -- ENTRY is ours, needed
! only as the END operand.
! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)16163.0
ENTRY   DL(U), FPK28                           ! F211A3: acc exp + +256
        C0011(BU,48), FPK28+.12, 20
        SLO(U), ROS
        L(BU), FPK44
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4                  ! test result exp+208, fract+1 s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BZB, ROS+.60, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
        DL(U), FPK38                           ! F211A4: acc exp + +50
        C0011(BU,48), FPK38+.12, 20
        SLO(U), ROS
        L(BU), FPK39
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4                  ! check opnd with exponent + +2
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BZB, ROS+.60, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                                 ! 016201.00: where F211A5 begins
        END, ENTRY
